    [
     1,
     "Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to create a model using mirt&#39;s multiple group function.</div><div>My code is quite simple:</div><div><br></div><div><div>items &lt;- c()</div><div>for (column in colnames(df))</div><div>     if (startsWith(column, &quot;Item&quot;)) items &lt;- append(items, column)</div></div><div><br></div><div><div>modelDf &lt;- rbind(df[df$grp == 0, items], df[df$grp == 1, items])</div><div>group &lt;- as.factor(df[,&quot;grp&quot;])</div></div><div><div>model &lt;- mirt::multipleGroup(data = modelDf, model = 1, itemtype=&quot;3PL&quot;, group = group)</div></div><div><br></div><div>However, I keep getting this error:</div><div><i>Multiple Group model will not be identified without proper constraints (groups contain missing data patterns where item responses have been completely omitted or, alternatively, the number of categories within each group is not equal to the total number of categories)</i><br></div><div><i><br></i></div><div>I&#39;ve gone through my dataframe multiple times but cannot seem to find the problems mentioned? What am I missing here?</div><div><br></div><div>The data frame (df) is shown below. It has only 6 rows.</div><div><br></div><div><img alt=\"df.PNG\" width=\"534px\" height=\"42px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/mirt-package/attach/139c92dd70a8e/df.PNG?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div><div><br>The data frame is also included in the attachments as a csv.</div><div><br></div><div>If anyone could point me out what is it I am missing it would be of great help (for me it seems the groups are fine!).<i><br></i></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Pedro</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
